panfrost/kmod: the kbase backend, and backend hooks for command streams and limits

- Registers the pan_kmod backend for Arm's mali_kbase (src/panfrost/lib/kmod/kbase_kmod.c,
  kbase_kmod_sync.c, kbase_kmod_csf.c, copied into the tree from userland/mesa-kbase/ by
  build-panvk.sh) after the DRM backends, and builds it.
- Adds three optional pan_kmod_ops: `ioctl` (the panthor command-stream ioctls a CSF user issues:
  group create/destroy/submit/get-state and tiler heap create/destroy), `get_csif_props` and
  `get_flush_id`, with pan_kmod_dev_ioctl(), pan_kmod_dev_get_csif_props() and
  pan_kmod_dev_get_flush_id() that fall back to the panthor fd and helpers when a backend has
  none. Panthor and panfrost are unchanged.
- Adds pan_kmod_dev_props.limits for what a backend cannot do: map a BO at more than one GPU VA,
  place a CPU mapping, share BOs or syncobjs as fds. All false for the DRM backends.
- Adds PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_GPU_SYNC for BOs holding sync objects command streams wait on (kbase
  re-evaluates such waits of a suspended group only in its CSF event memory), pan_kmod_bo.fixed_va
  for a BO the backend placed itself at allocation, and an optional `notify_sync_update` op with
  pan_kmod_dev_notify_sync_update() to tell the kernel the CPU changed such sync objects. No DRM
  backend offers the flag or the op; their behaviour is unchanged.

